Z||000000||84_duke||12-02-2001||11:55 PM||||How do I tell if my 84 has the better 4.10 ratio tranny in it, as opposed to the weaker 3.?? one?  Are there markings somewhere under the hood or something?<BR>Thanks<BR><P>------------------<BR>84_duke||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||12-03-2001||12:30 AM||||The 3.32 4-sp has the RPO code MY8 and the 4.10 is M19.<P>Only base model '84 Fieros had the 3.32, so if you have any options at all (sunroof, air, power anything, etc.) then you have the 4.10.  If you have an SE or an Indy then it will have the 4.10 as well.<P>Check out the sticker on the inner fender (under the hood) and look for the RPO code to be sure.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||NOCONES||12-03-2001||12:43 AM||||Or if it runs 3,000 rpm at 65 you got the 4.10.. i wish it had a fifth gear just kinda tagged on  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  but still it squeeks 30mpg out of that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>NOCONES<BR>-84 2M4 <BR>-4.10 4-speed<BR>-SCCA sollo II <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Nocones_1.jpg"> <P>Addmit it... it's just as much fun alone...  Solo II||||reg||1
